A||||1||Steve Normington||Leaking Half-Shaft Seal||||1||
Z||000000||Steve Normington||06-01-2001||08:29 PM||||I got a pair of the transmission needle bearing seals that the Fiero Store sells. (These are the bearings that replace the half-shaft seals in the transaxle case.) They are leaking oil like a British car. The leak seems to be around where the bearing goes into the case, not around the seal. Apart from removing the bearings and RTVing them, do you have any suggestions as to what I can do to eliminate this leak? If I need to remove these bearings, is there an easy way to do this with the transmission in the car and without removing the half-shafts?<P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierosound||06-02-2001||05:57 PM||||I had the same problem.  Apparently, the trans case seat for the seals isn't perfectly round.  A thin film of RTV is required when assembling to prevent leaks.<P>I don't think you can remove the bearing/seals without damaging them.  You may have to buy a new set.  <P>They can be replaced without dropping the transmission.  You will have to unbolt the lower control arms and torque struts to pull the half shafts from the transmission. A puller will be required to get the bearing/seals out.  <P>I had the Trans Shop that rebuilt my tranny do it.  Will cost 2-3 hours labour plus the bearing/seals.<BR>||||reg||10
